Package: proxy-scaler
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: proxy-scaler maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Depends: adduser
Description: MTG proxy card upscaling server
 Runs the proxy-scaler API and its generation worker as a managed pair,
 so the proxy-scaler desktop app (or any HTTP client) can queue card
 upscaling work against this machine's CPU or GPU.
 .
 The bundled runtime is self-contained — Python, PyTorch and the model
 loader are frozen into /opt/proxy-scaler, so no system Python or pip
 packages are required.
 .
 The API is UNAUTHENTICATED. The service ships bound to all interfaces
 so it is reachable from other machines; restrict it to a trusted
 network, or set PROXY_SCALER_SERVER_HOST=127.0.0.1 in
 /etc/default/proxy-scaler.
